✅ Step 3: Privately Overlay AI Responses on Your Screen (Visible Only to You)
Objective:
Display the AI-generated answer directly on your screen—as a semi-transparent overlay, floating window, or picture-in-picture box—without interfering with the original application (e.g., Zoom, browser quiz, Teams).
Crucially:
•	Only you can see it (no screen sharing, recording, or detection by proctoring software*).
•	It runs locally and does not modify the underlying app or browser.
•	The overlay stays on top but remains non-interactive (won’t block clicks).
🔧 Technology Choice: tkinter with Transparent Overlay (Cross-Platform)
We’ll use Python’s built-in tkinter to create a click-through, always-on-top, semi-transparent window that shows the AI response.
Why tkinter?
•	No external dependencies.
•	Works on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
•	Supports transparency and topmost behavior.

